/T (The `--input_fp16_nodes` parameter in the ATC tool is used to specify the name of an input node that has input data of type FP16 \(half-precision floating point\). This parameter is mutually exclusive with `--insert_op_conf`. When this parameter is set, it indicates that there is an input node in the original model that provides FP16 data. This is particularly useful when the input data to the model is expected to be in FP16 format, and the model needs to handle such inputs appropriately. Here are some key points about the `--input_fp16_nodes` parameter:)
/E (The `--input_fp16_nodes` parameter in the ATC tool is used to specify the name of an input node that has input data of type FP16 \(half-precision floating point\). This parameter is mutually exclusive with `--insert_op_conf`. When this parameter is set, it indicates that there is an input node in the original model that provides FP16 data. This is particularly useful when the input data to the model is expected to be in FP16 format, and the model needs to handle such inputs appropriately. Here are some key points about the `--input_fp16_nodes` parameter:)
