<<
/Title (How is the NC1HWC0 5D tensor format structured and what does C0 represent for FP16?)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1188 0 R
/Next 1243 0 R
>>
endobj
1212 0 obj
<<
/Title (This means that the C dimension is divided by 16, and any remainder is padded with zeros to align with the C0 size. In summary, for FP16 data type, C0 is 16, and C1 is calculated as \(C+15\)//16, ensuring that the data is stored consecutively in memory.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1188 0 R
/Prev 1244 0 R
>>
